# The MSVC toolset (major.minor) that builds the Windows release, checked by
# stage-msvc-runtime.ps1 against $env:VCToolsVersion in release.yml's
# build-windows job: the release fails when the toolset differs.
#
# Why it is pinned: the Windows agent carries the Visual C++ runtime app-local
# in its bin directory, and agent self-update (OTA) replaces only
# yuzu-agent.exe, never that runtime (#8219, decision #8218). An executable
# built by a newer toolset can need runtime exports the copy already on a
# device lacks, and then does not start. Holding the toolset fixed keeps every
# OTA-delivered executable within the runtime that devices already have.
#
# Bumping it is a deliberate, reviewed change. Its changelog fragment and
# release notes must say that devices updated by OTA across the bump also need
# the new installer or zip (which refreshes the runtime), until #8219/#8218
# change what OTA delivers. Keep docs/windows-build.md's toolchain table and
# the Wee Tam runner (deploy/windows/README.md) on the same toolset.
14.44
